{
  "_notes": [
    "Corne keymap v2. Edit this file, then run: python3 make_vil.py",
    "Keycodes are Vial spellings. Common ones: KC_A..KC_Z, KC_1..KC_0, KC_F1..KC_F12,",
    "KC_TRNS (transparent, does what the layer below does), KC_NO (dead key),",
    "LSFT(KC_1) for ! (shifted symbols are Shift + the base key: LSFT(KC_9) is '('),",
    "MO(3) hold for layer 3, LT1(KC_ESC) tap Esc / hold layer 1, LGUI_T(KC_CAPS) tap Caps Lock / hold Cmd.",
    "Row order: top, home, bottom. Left rows read outer -> pinky -> ring -> middle -> index -> inner.",
    "Right rows read inner -> index -> middle -> ring -> pinky -> outer.",
    "extra = [upper, lower]. left_thumbs = [outer, middle, inner]. right_thumbs = [inner, middle, outer].",
    "Layers not listed here are written as all KC_TRNS.",
    "Layer 4 mouse: Nav + Space toggles it on; Esc or a tap of the Nav key toggles it off.",
    "Number lock: Nav + Backspace thumb toggles layer 2 on; a tap of the Backspace thumb toggles it off.",
    "TD(0) is the Ctrl thumb: tap or hold for Ctrl, double tap for Ctrl+Space."
  ],
